  "job": "Tilts a pane of dawnglass that disarms the fighters swinging at his team.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "lore": "Ardit's pavise was a window once, the east pane of a Spire stair, taken down when the stair was cleared for the Dawn Arch road. He carried the glass out on his back and has not set it down since. Aubade children are told that a wall is a thing that waits; Ardit is a wall that turns, tilting the morning into the eyes of whoever lifts a blade. He apologises to the people he disarms. He means it, and he does it again a moment later. The dawn is on his side, and he will hold it open for anyone standing behind him.",
